Prior-art reference, not derived code
--------------------------------------

During analysis, this project's reference notes
(docs/deep-dive/ref-srtgo_plus.md) examined a local checkout of `srtgo_plus`,
a maintenance fork of `srtgo` (https://github.com/lapis42/srtgo). Per that
checkout's own LICENSE file, `srtgo_plus` is MIT-licensed (Copyright (c) 2023
DKim) and itself bundles two third-party components as reference: `SRT`
(MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Gyeongjae Choi) and `korail2`
(BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2014 Taehoon Kim; its KTX-handling module carries
that attribution in its own file header).

Those projects' request/response shapes for the KORAIL mobile API — endpoint
paths, form and query parameter names, and similar externally observable
facts — are exactly that: facts about how the KORAIL app and server
communicate, independently confirmed here against the decompiled KORAIL
Android application. This project's reference notes record those facts. No
source code, comments, or class/function structure were copied from
`srtgo_plus`, `srtgo`, `SRT`, or `korail2` into this package; the
`korail_mobile_api` implementation is this project's own, written from the
decompiled application. See docs/deep-dive/ref-srtgo_plus.md §1.1 for the
full analysis this notice summarizes.
